  "narrative": "The new independence contrasts materially strengthen the central dataset-level associations. KEAP1 loss remains a very large positive association after excluding PTEN loss and after excluding SMARCA4 loss (R27: +0.863 [0.796, 0.930]; R28: +0.822 [0.761, 0.882]), so KEAP1 loss is not a proxy for either PTEN loss or SMARCA4 loss in these analyses. SMARCA4 loss remains a very large negative raw association after excluding PTEN loss (R29: signed +0.845 [0.776, 0.914] for the negative-direction claim), reinforcing that it is not merely a PTEN co-mutation proxy. TP53 loss is now much better supported as an independent positive association: it remains far above the 0.15-unit threshold when KEAP1 loss is excluded (R32: +0.367 [0.265, 0.468]), when SMARCA4 loss is excluded (R33: +0.444 [0.346, 0.542]), and especially in the stringent joint exclusion of KEAP1 and SMARCA4 loss (R31: +0.402 [0.302, 0.502]). PTEN loss is independently supported when TP53 loss is excluded (R34: +0.259 [0.169, 0.349]), but the separate independence contrasts excluding KEAP1 loss (R30) or SMARCA4 loss (R35) have point estimates above threshold while their lower bounds are just below 0.15, so those specific independence claims remain unresolved. The CDKN2A contrast excluding TP53 and MTAP loss remains near threshold (R36: +0.142 [0.059, 0.224]), so it remains unresolved and active. MTAP loss excluding TP53 loss does not support the registered negative association and is near null (R37: -0.020 [-0.092, 0.053]); SMAD4 loss also does not support a negative association and is below threshold (R38: +0.036 [-0.073, 0.146]). These conclusions are associations in the supplied dataset, not causal effects or external generalizability, and the discovery contrasts overlap in sample so are not independent replications. I request independent validation for the central SMARCA4-loss claim H8 because it has the largest effect magnitude among the accepted associations but has not yet had independent validation.",
